<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry V of England</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1386">1386</a>–<a href="/years/1422">1422</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Henry V, Henry of Monmouth</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry V was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, Lord of Ireland and Duke of Aquitaine from 1413 until his death in 1422. The eldest son of Henry IV, he gained military experience in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> against the Glyndŵr rebellion and fought at the Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shrewsbury">Shrewsbury</a> when only 16. In 1415 he renewed the war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, besieged Harfleur and won at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-agincourt">Agincourt</a>, then from 1417 set out to conquer Normandy. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-troyes">Treaty of Troyes</a> of 1420 made him regent and heir to Charles VI, but Henry died in August 1422, seven weeks before Charles, and was succeeded by the infant Henry VI.</p></div>
